; Host Node.js Server (Short Notes)

; =======================================================================================

; Localhost server is accessible only on our computer

; To make APIs accessible to all users, server must be hosted online

; Hosting makes application available 24×7 on the Internet

; Cloud companies provide server + storage + network

; Some platforms are paid, some offer free tier for developers

; 🚀 Popular Platforms to Host Node.js Applications
; 🔹 Free / Developer-Friendly Platforms

; Render – Easy, free tier, good for Node.js & MongoDB

; Railway – Simple deployment, limited free credits

; Cyclic – Free Node.js hosting (good for APIs)

; Glitch – Small demo projects

; Fly.io – Free tier, Docker-based

; Deta Space – Free micro apps (limited)

; 🔹 Paid / Cloud Platforms

; AWS (EC2 / Elastic Beanstalk) – Powerful but costly & complex

; Google Cloud Platform (GCP) – Scalable, paid

; Microsoft Azure – Enterprise-level hosting

; DigitalOcean – Affordable VPS

; Vercel – Best for frontend + serverless APIs

; Netlify – Frontend + serverless functions

; ⭐ Best Choice for Students / Beginners

; ✅ Render

; ✅ Railway

; ✅ Cyclic